---
source: tests/cli/completions.rs
expression: help
---
print a script that lets a shell complete fetchloom's commands and options

usage: fetchloom completions [options] <shell>

arguments:
  <shell>  the shell that loads the script [possible values: bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh]

options:
  -q, --quiet         print only the answer and errors
  -v, --verbose...    say more: -v adds detail and counters, -vv adds debug logs
      --json          print one JSON document on stdout instead of the story
      --offline       use only what is already on this machine
  -y, --yes           approve confirmations, but never choose a dataset for you
      --color <when>  when to use color [default: auto] [possible values: auto, always, never]
  -C <dir>            run as if fetchloom started in <dir>
  -h, --help          print help

examples:
  fetchloom completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/fetchloom
  fetchloom completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_fetchloom
  fetchloom completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/fetchloom.fish
  fetchloom completions powershell | Out-String | Invoke-Expression

on disk: nothing. it prints the script on stdout, for a file your shell loads
